# Task Execution

Treat the selected task specification as the implementation contract.

Before coding:

- verify the task ID;
- inspect dependencies;
- inspect referenced ADRs;
- inspect referenced architecture;
- inspect API/data contracts;
- inspect existing code and patterns;
- identify security and accessibility implications.

During coding:

- do not silently change architectural boundaries;
- do not bypass authorization because a UI hides an action;
- do not trust browser-supplied tenant identifiers;
- do not introduce real PHI;
- do not add a dependency when an existing project capability is sufficient;
- keep vertical slices complete across the relevant layers.

If the task conflicts with an ADR or security requirement:

1. stop the conflicting implementation;
2. explain the conflict;
3. propose the documentation/ADR change;
4. continue only after the decision is clear.

After coding:

- verify every acceptance criterion;
- run appropriate lint/type-check/tests;
- inspect loading/empty/error states;
- inspect accessibility;
- inspect authorization/tenant boundaries;
- report changed files and any deviations;
- update task completion information.
